3 CITY Engestofte
3 CTRY Denmark
1 DEAT
2 DATE 15 NOV 1634
2 ADDR
3 CITY Pederstrup
3 CTRY Denmark
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Born on Engestofte, Lolland 1599, left for Halle (Sachsen, Germany) at the age of 15; in 1619 he participated in an expedition to Spitzbergen where he learned the art of navigation.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joined the Florence-navy in battles against the Turks.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Maren Steensen til Steensgaard, whose sister Anne Steensen, was married to Joachim's brother Kjøn Jochum.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joachims daughter Barbara Grabow and her husband Lauritz Galtung are ancestors to the Russian poet A.J.Pusjkin!!
2 CONT
2 CONT In 'Rigsarkivet' in Kobenhavn there is a handwritten book by Joachim, containing births, deaths and marriages of his family as well as a description of his life.
2 CONT
2 CONT 'Personalhistorisk Tidsskrift', 1890, contains a transcript of the funeral speech held when Joachim was burried in 1634.
2 CONT
2 CONT See further Elin Galtung Lihaugs website http://www.norge.ru/file/public_doc/Landsmann_om_Pusjkin.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT Kilde: Roskilde Historie: Joachim Grabow  ~ Maren Steensen Hans Hansen  ~ Merethe Pedersdatter Uf   
2 CONT   til Wuticke,  Sørup til Sørup til Pederstrup, Maribo af Steensgård  von Holstein af Simblegård   
2 CONT   & Ottestrup   Myregård & Simblegård, Bornholm ~ Nakskov 15/5 1625 til Simblegård, Klemensker ~ 1606   
2 CONT   Dansk Skibsløjtnant 1624     Deltager ekspedition til Spitzbergen   * Simblegård 1566 † 1638   
2 CONT   Skibschef 1628   Florentisk tjeneste mod tyrkiske galajer    
2 CONT   Lensmand Borreby & Jerrestad Herred, Skåne 1640     
2 CONT
2 CONT    * Engestofte 18/10 1599 † 1634 
