2 CONT Notes: Notes by Holger Hertzum:  Mr. Anders Jachimsen or Jacobsen Voergaard (Hellum H.) met in 1449 to change after His grandfather, was 1,460 knight and then blue. a. present in Aarhus at settlement mellern the Rosenkrantzer and 
2 CONC Lave Brock, gave in 1466 with his wife Gods to Holy House in Aalborg, held in 1475 Switch with its cousins, the 1481 Counselor, sealed in 1487 homage in Lund, was forlehnet with Hellum Herred, did in 1490 his will and † p. A. afte
2 CONC r ample to have hesitated churches and convents; GM Anne Lauridsdatter Muus (with a mill wheel of the weapon) to the Stenalt (Rugsø H.); they had chosen 1467 to a burial in Randers Klosterkirke, but now in a square Stenalts Sognek
2 CONC irke Oersted, 1492 Switching maintained by them.  Children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT a) Mr. Jacob or Joachim Andersen Voergaard mentioned in 1480 as Medudsteder of a witness of Skovby Herreds Thing was 1484 Hofsinde, lay in 1486 in Borgeleie in Dalby Monastery in Scania and 1492 at Antvorskov, founded p. A. with h
2 CONC is brothers Requiems the Father wrote himself in 1496 to Tybjerg (Tybjerg H.) as Medudsteder of a witness in Zealand Country Thing, was 1,501 forlehnet with Gaunø and had also Jerslev, Vennebjerg and Hollum Herreder in Forlehning,
2 CONC  the last was him, however fradømt 1505, was in 1503 counselor, 1505 Sending the meeting in Kalmar, 1509 present at the negotiations in Copenhagen with the Swedish, also in 1513, was 1,511 vassal of Annisse and as yet only a squir
2 CONC e, but in 1512 Knight when he was present at the king's entree Thing in Randers, 1516 forlehnet with Nørlyng District, wrote himself in 1522 to Støvringgaard (Støvring H.), was † 1525; g. prior to 1496 m. Margrete Poulsdatter (Fik
2 CONC kesen?) to Tybjerggård that 1525 was the widow and the exchange of real acquired his relative Erik Mogensen (Mormand) of the Part of Tybjerggård and still alive on Støvringgaard 1555, when she is present in Rust Service books.  Ch
2 CONC ildren: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1) Anders Jacobsen to Voergaard and Støvringgaard, was 1528 with the grated to follow the king abroad, led 1535 Process against her cousin Anders Bjørnsen, was p. A. Provisioning Master, were still alive in 1536, was forl. m. Else
2 CONC be Grubbe, but died before the wedding. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2) Dorte to Tybjerggård and Støvringgaard, were still alive in 1562; g. 1. m. Christopher substances Hack to Egholm, b. 1488 † 1539 as his family's last man, g. 2. m. Oluf Glob to Vellumgaard that was † 1558.  b) Bjørn Andersen to
2 CONC  Stenalt led 1490 Tired with Markvard Skjernov on Værgemaalet Axel Jepsen (Thott) 's Children, founded in 1492 with his brothers Sjæle- fairs were 1,502 present and complicit when Ebbe Strangesen on Høibro killed butler Mr. Poul L
2 CONC axmand were 1,505 present at the king's entree Thing in Copenhagen, 1506 forlehnet with Rugsø Herred and 1,507 vassal of Ravnsborg; GM Anne Friis (from Haraldskjaer) Henriksdattcr to the point, † 1542 (she g. 2. m. hr. Ove Lung (e
2 CONC xpensive) to Tirsbæk, † 22 Febr. 1540); both limited. Church of Our Lady in Aalborg. Children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1) Anders Bjørnsen to Stenalt recruited in 1525 in a Rust Rostering to ask four Gla wind, 1527-36 forlehnet with Rugsø District, was in 1528 promised to follow the King abroad; GM Anne Gjordsdatter (Drefeld); both limited. in Chur
2 CONC ch Oersted. Sun: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Bjørn Andersen, see the newer generation.  2) Henrik Bjørnsen Stenalt to include in the recess 1536, 1536-41 was forlehnet with Rugsø District, led in 1537 with Process Holy houses in Aalborg and Randers lived in Nov. 1540, but wa
2 CONC s soon after killed by Heinrich Blome. The shift was maintained in 1541; GM its cousin Anne Johansdatter (bear) (she g. 2. m. Christoffer Johansen Lindenov to Drenderup). 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3) Anne, † 1540, GM Niels Kaas (with a Sparre of the weapon) to the Thaarup Overgaard, † 1035.  c) Yep Andersen Muus to Randrup (Hellum H), founded in 1492 soul fairs, was 1493 Hofsinde, founded in 1509 Messer in Holy house in Ran
2 CONC ders, certainly † unmarried.  d) Erik Andersen probably † small.  e) Niels Andersen probably † small.  f) Margaret, 1495 lived on Støvringgaard, GM Axel Jepsen, (Thott) to Støvringgaard, was † 1490; on Værgemaalet and legacy of th
2 CONC eir minds weak daughter were brought great strife between the Bjørn'er and Axel's kinsmen.  g) Sophie, GM Herman Fleming to Bavelse (he g. 2. m. Anne Eriksdatter Thott).  h) Inger to Randrup, g. 1. m. Niels Jensen (Munk with the v
2 CONC ine of the weapon) to the Visborg that led main banner in Slagct by Brunkebjerg but died shortly after 2 m. Jens Tygesen (Seefeld) to Dalsgaard.  i) Anne, GM Eight Emmiksen to Refsø. 
