1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =='''Peder Eilersen Brockenhuus (c. 1544 - before April 28, 1608)'''==
2 CONT
2 CONT Was a Dano-Norwegian nobleman, landowner, and naval officer. He played a significant role in the administration of fiefs (lens) in Østfold and Hedmark during the late 16th century.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Biography and Career:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Peder was the son of '''Eiler Henriksen Brockenhuus''' († 1546) and '''Kirsten Eriksdatter Gyldenhorn of Elingård'''. His career spanned court service and naval administration:
2 CONT
2 CONT * In 1572–1573, he served as a court page (hofjunker) at the Danish court.
2 CONT * In 1579, he was called to sea service, and in 1583, he was appointed as a ship commander (skibshøvedsmand).
2 CONT * In 1583, he was granted the fief of Skjeberg, including the Melby estate.
2 CONT * In 1586, he was discharged from his position as a naval commander.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Estates and Financial Transactions:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Peder owned extensive lands, including the manors of [https://lokalhistoriewiki.no/wiki/Hovinsholm_(Ringsaker_gnr._535/1) Hovindsholm] (in Hedmark) and Sanne/Evjegård (in Østfold).
2 CONT
2 CONT * Peder frequently used his lands as collateral for loans, primarily from his relatives in the Juel family.
2 CONT * In 1598, he transferred the Evjegård estate to Lady '''Dorthe Juel''', likely as part of a settlement for a debt of 3,000 rigsdaler.
2 CONT * These transactions allowed him to maintain liquidity while keeping core family estates within the kinship circle.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Family:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT After 1580, Peder was married to '''Elsebe Mogensdatter Juel''' († 1602). There is no information about this couple having children together. Peder's supposed illegitimate daughter was, '''Sippora''', who married (1589) the clergy
2 CONC man '''Jens Bugge''', followed strict Scandinavian naming traditions for her sons, supporting their connection to the Brockenhuus clan.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sources:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://books.google.ru/books?id=FV6UvjkkD9gC&printsec=frontcover&hl=ru#v=onepage&q&f=false Danmarks Adels Aarbog 1897, s. 91.]
2 CONT # Thiset, Hiort-Lorenzen, Bobé, Teisen, [https://slaegtsbibliotek.dk/2024/941649.pdf Danmarks Adels Aarbog, (Dansk Adelsforening 1884-2020), DAA 1962:II:10], 62 b. P. 397.
2 CONT # [https://genealogi.no/3d-flip-book/genealogen-2004-nr-2/ A.S. Langekiehl. Genealogen 2004/2: Slektene på Skog i Skiptvet og Søgård i Øymark.] P. 44-45.
2 CONT # [https://slaegtsbibliotek.dk/920458.pdf Albert Fabritius. Slægten Brockenhuus], 1958. P. 14.
