1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Denne gamle sjællandske Slægt, hvis Vaaben var en gaaende Vildbasse i Skjoldet — oprindelig over tre Bølger, hvis man kan stole paa Klevenfeldts Afbildning af Hr. Herluf Jakobsens nu tabte Sigil — paa Hjelmen to Ve
2 CONC sselhorn (jvf. D. Adel. Sig. 88, 448—49), kan man kun i Mangel af et andet Slægtnavn tillægge Navnet Grubbe; thi, saavidt vides, var det kun Hr. Herluf s to Sønner Peder og Jakob, der benyttede dette Tilnavn, vistnok en mødrene Ar
2 CONC v, medens hans tredie Søn Bo, troligvis af lignende Aarsag, kaldte sig Bo Dyre; baade Grubbe- og Dyre-Navnet synes desuden at være gaaet af Brug i denne Slægt ved de nævnte tre Brødres Død.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Slight translation in english:
2 CONT
2 CONT This old Zealand family, whose weapon was a wild bore in the shield - originally over three waves, if you can count on Klevenfeldt's image of Mr. Herluf Jakobsens now lost Sigil - on Hjelmen two Vesselhorn (cf. D. Adel, Sig. 88, 4
2 CONC 48-49), only in the absence of another family name can be added the name Grubbe; for, as you know, it was only Mr. Herluf's two sons Peder and Jakob, who used this nickname, probably a mother's inheritance, while his third son Bo,
2 CONC  probably for similar reasons, called himself Dyer; Both the grubbe and Dyerl name also seem to have been used in this genus by the death of the three mentioned brothers.
2 CONT
2 CONT Geography
2 CONT
2 CONT * Definitions of Zealand
2 CONT * noun
2 CONT * the principal island of Denmark, located between the Jutland peninsula and the southern tip of Sweden. Its chief city is Copenhagen.
